# Dependencies
node_modules/

# The three provider packages under vendor/ are DeepSeek's own published npm packages. They are NOT
# committed here (committing them would re-distribute somebody else's package). They are fetched at
# install time by `scripts/fetch-vendor.mjs`, which runs from the `prepare` lifecycle script — the
# only lifecycle hook npm/pnpm execute for a git dependency.
#
# Note the shape of these rules: an ignore pattern with no negation is fine here (unlike the
# packages/bundle case in some sibling repos) because pnpm building the git-dependency file list from
# .gitignore is exactly what we WANT — the vendor content has no business being inside the packed
# tarball. `prepare` reconstructs it after unpacking.
vendor/browser-use/
vendor/browser-use-runtime/
vendor/browser-use-chrome-devtools-mcp/

# Package artifacts
*.tgz

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

